name c01m08-volcanic-nightmare
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T22:21:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 8 OF 10 -- {Volcanic Nightmare}* [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: 19 of 20 objects -- 12 T-80s and 7 Werewolves -- "by killing them all". A pure
# clear-the-board, and campaign.md 8 nominates it as the campaign's cheapest regression probe.
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 3 (Ka'u Desert, Hawaii, terrain.md 6), day -- sun +56.61 deg at the lead's
# spawn, computed by the runner. 19 starred objects, unlock marker *.
# THE CAST: 7 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 12 T-80 -> `target_hard` - wingman -> `f16`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 8, Stinger 8, artillery 8, wingman 10, fuel
# 8000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 40` = 8000 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all 19 starred objects. campaign.md 8 nominates this file as the campaign's
#   cheapest regression probe -- a pure clear-the-board with no fuel constraint, no artillery, no
#   schedule and no SAM -- so if anything in weapons or damage drifts, THIS is the file that moves
#   first, and its met count is the number to watch.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading; report the met count against 19.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): FOUR OF NINETEEN.
#   t = 21.5 / 24.7 s   two Mk-82 away, aimErrM 14.44 (`two`, at t05) and 7.73 (`lead`, at t01)
#   the 14.44 m MISSES  `target_hard` needs about 8 m to be finished, so `two`'s bomb kills nothing and
#                       the whole yield is `lead`'s single hit on the four-T-80 stack at 230,450. This
#                       is the file that shows the fragility class doing its job
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 4 of 19 met, `survive` met; `two` SUCCESS. No SAM.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m08 1
  spawn 19.38269 -155.28829 150 313.5 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 40
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 19.41419 -155.32353 150 300
  wp 19.43817 -155.35037 1000 300
  objective kill unit t01
  objective kill unit t02
  objective kill unit t03
  objective kill unit t04
  objective kill unit t05
  objective kill unit t06
  objective kill unit t07
  objective kill unit t08
  objective kill unit t09
  objective kill unit t10
  objective kill unit t11
  objective kill unit t12
  objective kill unit w01
  objective kill unit w02
  objective kill unit w03
  objective kill unit w04
  objective kill unit w05
  objective kill unit w06
  objective kill unit w07
  objective survive

